# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this template is committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # then set a strong ADMIN_PASSWORD (see below)
#
# ADMIN_PASSWORD — REQUIRED for `docker compose up`.
#
# main.go:104 refuses to start when the stored admin password is still the default
# `changeme` AND the bind host is non-loopback. docker-compose.yml sets HOST=0.0.0.0,
# so this guard always applies to the Docker deployment. Without it the container
# crash-loops with:
#
#   Refusing to start: admin password is still the default on a non-loopback host (0.0.0.0)
#
# The error message also offers "or bind to 127.0.0.1" — that escape does NOT work in
# Docker, because a container-loopback listener is unreachable through the published
# port mapping. Setting this variable is the only viable fix here.
#
# This value is the password for the /admin panel. It is an env override only:
# config.SetPassword keeps it in `passwordOverride`, which Save() never writes into
# data/config.json, so the secret stays out of the config file and out of
# /admin/api/config/export.
#
# Generate one:
#   python3 -c "import secrets,string;print(''.join(secrets.choice(string.ascii_letters+string.digits) for _ in range(40)))"
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Optional: publish the proxy on a different host port (container always listens on 8080).
#KIRO_PORT=8080

# Optional: host path to the Kiro IDE AWS SSO cache directory, mounted read-only so the
# containerized app can import the IDE credential. Defaults to ${HOME}/.aws/sso/cache.
#KIRO_AWS_SSO_CACHE_DIR=/home/you/.aws/sso/cache
